## Founding & History
Clover Hill Wines was established in 1986 on the site of an old dairy farm in north-east Tasmania, with the explicit goal of producing premium sparkling wines. The winery was founded by the Goelet family from America, who also owned Taltarni in Victoria and founded Clos du Val in Napa Valley. In September 2024, Clover Hill, along with its sister winery Taltarni, was acquired by the Fogarty and Hall families through their company, Tasmania East Coast Vineyards Pty Ltd. Peter Fogarty is the founder of the family-controlled Fogarty Wine Group, and Anthony Hall holds significant seafood interests across Australia and Tasmania.

## People
The chief winemaker at Clover Hill Wines since 2019 is Robert Heywood. Ben Howell is also listed as a winemaker. Adam Torpy served as CEO of Clover Hill Wines in December 2019. The Goelet family were the founders and previous owners. The current ownership transitioned to the Fogarty and Hall families in late 2024. Outgoing CEO Michael Kluczko expressed satisfaction that the brands would be "shepherded" by a family group.

## Vineyard & Site
Clover Hill is located in Lebrina, Pipers River, in north-east Tasmania. The vineyard spans 23.9 hectares. The broader property, encompassing the winery and architecturally designed cellar door, is nearly 68 hectares. The vineyard is planted exclusively with the traditional sparkling wine varieties of Chardonnay, Pinot Noir, and Pinot Meunier. The site benefits from a cool, frost-free maritime climate, ancient volcanic soils, and a sheltered, naturally sloping amphitheatre. The soil is described as red rocky volcanic, averaging 1-5 meters deep, scattered with basalt stone, and is free-draining with high organic matter and nutrient-holding capacity. Vines are planted 1.1 meters apart, with 1.9 meters between rows. Northeast sites, close to Bass Strait, experience strong maritime influences, while hillside slopes offer protection from prevailing westerly winds, fostering warm, settled, and relatively dry growing conditions.

## Cellar Door Experience
The Clover Hill cellar door is described as an "award-winning boutique cellar door". It operates Wednesday through Sunday from 11 AM to 4:30 PM. The cellar door's design reflects the brand's quality and adheres to three core principles: terroir, method, and blend. Wine critic Huon Hooke noted it as "without a doubt, the most impressive new cellar door" he encountered on a trip to Tasmania. The cellar door offers structured experiences, such as a winter vine pruning masterclass, which includes a guided vineyard tour, hands-on pruning, a 15-year sparkling wine tasting masterclass, and a cheese platter. These experiences are exclusively for tasting and masterclass guests. There are also explorations for the Tasmanian Symphony Orchestra to perform at the cellar door.

## Food & Hospitality
While there is no mention of a full-service restaurant, a cheese platter is provided as part of the vine pruning masterclass experience. The winery also hosts corporate events.

## Awards & Recognition
Clover Hill Wines has received significant accolades, including Silver medallist in the 2019 Tasmanian Tourism Awards and a 5-star rating in the 2020 Halliday Wine Companion. The vineyard has been twice awarded Tasmanian Vineyard of the Year. Specific wine recognitions include 95 gold for Clover Hill Blanc de Blancs Multi-Vintage Non Vintage Sparkling, and 93 silver for both Clover Hill Riche Multi-Vintage Non Vintage Sparkling and Clover Hill Exceptionnelle Multi-Vintage. The Clover Hill Vintage Brut 2016 received 93 points out of 100 (silver ribbon) from The Real Review. The winery is acknowledged as one of Australia's finest sparkling producers and has garnered prestigious Australian and international awards and critical acclaim.

## Sustainability & Certifications
No reliable information found from public sources.

## Visiting Practical Info
Clover Hill Wines is located at 60 Clover Hill Road, Lebrina, Tas 7254. The winery is situated north of Launceston, along the Tamar Valley wine route. The phone number is (03) 6395 6114. The official website is www.cloverhillwines.com.au. Clover Hill wines are exported to the UK, the US, and other major markets.

## Notable / Distinctive
Clover Hill is distinguished as one of Australia's few premium sparkling houses dedicated solely to producing sparkling wines using the traditional method. The winery has been instrumental in redefining Tasmanian sparkling wine since its establishment in 1986. Its multi-vintage philosophy aims for a consistent house style. The cool climate and growing conditions in Tasmania are noted for their similarity to the Champagne region of France, contributing to the quality, elegance, and finesse of Clover Hill's sparkling wines. The cellar door has been recognized by wine critic Huon Hooke as "the most impressive new cellar door" he observed in Tasmania.

